# Archived snapshot: `docs/Clarified_Degeneracy_and_Majorant_Blocks.lean`

The original text of this file is preserved verbatim in the git history:

    git show b4001a7:docs/Clarified_Degeneracy_and_Majorant_Blocks.lean

(sha256 `847d2f78dbd93022a7e5f1ee594e6328fb0e2a3d14ed98ea9bce00ddd3fc896b`, listed in `historical/ARCHIVED_LEAN_SNAPSHOTS.md`).

That text was never compiled by the kernel-certificate build: it was outside the lake
libraries, and it contained 18 uses of `sorry`/`axiom` outside comments. It proves nothing and is not part of any claim.

This file now contains only this note, so that every tracked `.lean` file is compiled with
no `sorry` and no custom axiom. The kernel-checked development is the `NS_Millennium_Proof`
library; see `README.md`.
